##fileformat=VCFv4.3
##contig=<ID=chr1,length=1000000>
##META=<ID=Assay,Number=.,Type=String,Values=[A, B]>
##META=<ID=Assay,Number=.,Type=String,Values=[C, D]>
##Authority=hts-specs' own test/vcf/{4.1,4.2}/passed/passed_meta_contig.vcf fixture declares ##contig=<ID=1> then ##contig=<ID=1,length=123456> and is expected to parse successfully -- direct precedent that a duplicate declaration ID is not a structural violation in the spec's own conformance suite, extended here to ##META per DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Why this warns instead of throwing" section (the same rule applies uniformly across all seven keyed declaration types). ##fileformat=VCFv4.3 is required since ##META doesn't exist as a structured declaration type before VCFv4.3.
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1) keeps the first ##META=<ID=Assay,...,Values=[A, B]> declaration and silently drops the duplicate, exit 0, no warning -- BcftoolsDependencyTest#testDuplicateMetaIdBcftoolsKeepsFirst pins this live measurement; re-confirmed directly via bcftools view -h on 2026-08-16.
##Authority=vcf_validator 0.10.2 reports this file valid -- measured live via vcf_validator -i <file> -r summary,text on 2026-08-16, but ONLY with attributes ordered ID,Number,Type,Values as written here: its Ragel grammar's meta_meta rule (vcf-validator src/vcf/vcf_v43.ragel:138-141) hard-codes that exact order ('ID=' ... ',Number=' '.' ... ',Type=' 'String' ... ',Values=' '[' ... ']'). The ID,Type,Number,Values order BcftoolsDependencyTest#testDuplicateMetaIdBcftoolsKeepsFirst actually uses (matching VCFv4.3.tex:273's own worked example) was measured invalid ("Line 2: Error in META metadata.") for a single, non-duplicated declaration alone -- i.e. this is the same order-sensitivity HTS_SPECS_BASELINE_STATUS.md's "Metadata declaration fields declared out of canonical order" row already documents as a deliberately-unenforced vcf_validator quirk (no spec version requires an attribute order; vcf_validator rejects the spec's own example), not a new finding, and not evidence about this fixture's actual subject (duplicate-ID handling, which this library and bcftools apply identically regardless of attribute order). This fixture is deliberately ordered ID,Number,Type,Values purely so its own vcf_validator citation is genuine, per the "confirm the actual verdict... do not carry forward unverified" instruction this corpus follows.
##ExpectWarnContains=keeping the first declaration
##RoundTripDivergenceReason=VcfMetadata.Builder.addMeta() drops the second, duplicate ##META declaration when it detects the shared ID (DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's reference table); the writer then emits only the surviving first declaration, so the round trip is not byte-identical even though it is semantically equivalent -- verified live during authoring: only the second ##META line ("Values=[C, D]") is missing from the written output.
#CHROM	POS	ID	REF	ALT	QUAL	FILTER	INFO
chr1	1	rs1	A	T	.	PASS	.
